i purposely excluded the other weapons. those lawful characters sure
get neat toys. my interpretation of the attack numbers are (using
Excalibur for example) +5 to hit and upto 10 additional pts of damage
for a +0 sword. my questions are these: how does a war hammer rank
compared to a long sword? clearly Mjollnir enhances a war hammer more
than Excalibur does a long sword but is Mjollnir a better (crunching)
weapon? all of these weapons should be unattainable except as gifts.
in any event, i've found that a blessed +8 Frost Brand seems to be
plenty of trouble for the nasties. the thing to remember about +8 is
if your weapon is already better than +5 then don't enchant it ...

how about some named darts that have a confusion attack as well as a
better chance to hit and do more damage? missile weapons are mostly
useless as is. potions are more fun to heave ... perhaps dipping darts
into potions of confusion or paralyis could make them "treated" with a
chance that they'd exhibit that special attack. that could work against
you as well ...

